# stdlib/modules/db/index.lph
#
# index.lph — external-load manifest, read by the VM's loader
# (liphia_virtual_machine::external::VM::load_external_module).
#
# Unlike db.lph (the Liphia-facing docs / composed layer), this file is not
# compiled or executed as Liphia source — it is a small line-oriented
# manifest telling the VM which prebuilt native library to load for this
# module's db_*/pg_* functions, instead of finding them statically
# compiled into the liphia_cli / liphia_cli_gui binary.
#
# Syntax: one instruction per line. '#' starts a comment; blank lines are
# ignored.
#
#   external "<library base name>"
#
# The named library is expected at:
#   lib/<platform prefix><name><platform suffix>
# e.g. lib/libliphia_module_db.so on Linux, lib/liphia_module_db.dll on
# Windows, lib/libliphia_module_db.dylib on macOS — resolved automatically,
# no need to list all three.
#
# Source of this library: liphia_engine/crates/liphia_module_db
# (SQLite via rusqlite "bundled" + a pure-TCP PostgreSQL wire-protocol
# client — see that crate for details).

external "liphia_module_db"
